<tr valign="top" height="400" >
<td tEditID="c1r1" style=" background-color:#FFFFFF; color:#000000; bEditID:r3st1; bLabel:main; font-size:12pt; font-family:arial;" aEditID="c1r1" locked="0" >
<![CDATA[<div style=""><font face="arial">Hello <span style="background-color: rgb(255, 255, 0);">client name</span>,</font></div><div style=""><font face="arial">I hope you are well and having a great fall season. As we get close to the end of the year, I’d like to remind you of the upcoming email communication sent out by our Section 125 Team (email sent from the address Insperity Benefits <a href="&lt;InsperityBenefits@response.insperity.com&gt;"><b>&lt;InsperityBenefits@response.insperity.com&gt;</b></a>) prompting you to complete the required annual Section 125 Nondiscrimination Testing Questionnaire.</font></div><div style=""><font face="arial"><br></font></div><div style=""><font face="arial">This Nondiscrimination Questionnaire (NDQ) is an annual requirement as it supplies critical information for Insperity to perform IRS-required nondiscrimination testing on the Insperity Group Health, Health Care FSA and 401(k) plans. The questionnaire also is used to determine applicable large employer (ALE) status under the Affordable Care Act.</font></div><div style=""><font face="arial">&nbsp;</font></div><div style=""><font face="arial"><b><u>ALL</u></b> clients must submit this information annually for each Insperity client parent company (client ID numbers ending in 00).</font></div><div style=""><br></div><div style=""><font face="arial">Since you have an Insperity Group Health Plan and/or have access to the Insperity Health Care FSA, you will need to complete the questionnaire for Section 125 Nondiscrimination Testing even if you do not have an Insperity 401(k) plan. It is important that you complete the questionnaire in a timely manner so that your employees can maintain their pre-tax benefits.</font></div><div style=""><font face="arial"><br></font></div><div style=""><font face="arial">I have attached the PDF instructions for completing the questionnaire on Insperity Premier and included a summary below.&nbsp;</font></div><div style=""><font face="arial"><br></font></div><div style=""><font face="arial">•<span style="white-space:pre">	</span><a href="http://portal.insperity.com">Individuals with confidential security role</a> – Login in to <a href="http://portal.insperity.com">http://portal.insperity.com</a></font></div><div style=""><font face="arial">•<span style="white-space:pre">	</span>Click “Regulatory and Compliance” under Company</font></div><div style=""><font face="arial">•<span style="white-space:pre">	</span>Select "Section125 / Nondiscrimination Testing” under Government Reporting</font></div><div style=""><font face="arial">•<span style="white-space:pre">	</span>Select “Access Now”</font></div><div style=""><font face="arial">•<span style="white-space:pre">	</span>Select “Begin Questionnaire”</font></div><div style=""><font face="arial"><br></font></div><div style=""><font face="arial">If you’ve previously completed the questionnaire with Insperity, you will need to verify and/or update business information and submit it for plan year 2025.&nbsp;</font></div><div style=""><font face="arial"><br></font></div><div style=""><font face="arial">If you need assistance answering any portion of the questionnaire, we are here to help you. Please contact the Insperity Contact Center, option 1 at 866-715-3552 (weekdays between 7am and 7pm CST) and a team member can assist you.&nbsp;</font></div><div style=""><font face="arial"><br></font></div><div style=""><font face="arial">Sincerely,</font></div>]]></td>
</tr>
</table>